    <item>
      <title>Silvia Almada Monter wins Kippenhahn Prize</title>
      <link>http://asgard-ari.github.io/post/25-07-22-kippenhahn-prize/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 22 Jul 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://asgard-ari.github.io/post/25-07-22-kippenhahn-prize/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;















&lt;figure  &gt;
  &lt;div class=&#34;d-flex justify-content-center&#34;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&#34;w-100&#34; &gt;&lt;img src=&#34;http://asgard-ari.github.io/uploads/silvia-kippenhahn-attached.png&#34; alt=&#34;Silvia Almada Monter wins Kippenhahn Prize&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; data-zoomable /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Max Planck Institute for Astrophysics (MPA) has awarded the Rudolf-Kippenhahn-Prize for the best scientific paper by a student to Silvia Almada Monter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Silvia received the award for her paper titled &amp;ldquo;Crossing walls and windows: the curious escape of Lyman-α photons through ionized channels&amp;rdquo;. Her research challenges existing assumptions about how Lyman-alpha photons escape from galaxies, proposing a new physical picture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The prize recognizes originality, scientific impact, and the quality of writing in publications where students made substantial contributions.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
    </item>
    
